rod: persist per-element OSD changes + report element colour

set-element / show-element updated only the in-memory element, never the
shared config object, so `config save` never wrote per-element color,
font_size, position, visible, etc. A colour picked in the WebUI reverted to
white on the next boot. Mirror each runtime change into the [osd.<name>]
section via rss_config_set_str so a save persists it (rod already reads
these keys back on load).

Also add the effective text colour to the 'elements' list so a UI can show
the current colour instead of guessing white.

